WEBVTT

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.480
Bye-bye!

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:02.670
See you tomorrow!

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:05.860
Oh, I forgot!

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.070
Right?

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.060
Bye, Kidoma-sensei!

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.260
Bye-bye. See you tomorrow!

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:18.280
With a Gentle Face
 and Kind Words

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.070
Say, do you want to go get something to eat?

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:18.750
Huh?

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.700
Well, we couldn't go while 
we were doing our tests.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.250
Oh! Yeah, let's go!

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.090
How about that new curry place?

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.390
Oh, that sounds good. Let's go!

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:28.480
I can't wait!

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.310
Right?

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.000
Okay. That's all of them.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.220
We did a good job gathering
 all of these, meow.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:41.290
Now... we'll be able to build... 
our secret hideout... right?

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:44.050
Floorboards and walls... the roof...

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.910
These should cover most of that.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:47.140
I think.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.100
That's great!

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.170
Yes.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.600
Oh, that feels so nice!

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.840
So? What are we planning to do about those?

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.290
The TABs. The tree attachment bolts.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.460
How are we going to cover the extra cost?

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.990
We have no choice. 
We'll have to use this after—

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:09.060
Let's go to the beach.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:10.410
What?

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:11.510
The beach?!

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:13.980
That sounds nice! The beach!

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:16.960
Beach! Beach! Beach! Beach!

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.400
Everyone going somewhere together!

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.390
Why are we talking about going
 the beach instead of money?!

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.480
Why do you think?

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:01.530
<b>Step 6
"DIY" Means Dull, Unexciting Items Come in Handy!</b>

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.950
Thank you, Pudding.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.570
Today's lessons were interesting, too.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:05.860
Good job.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.170
Yes, yes.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:11.610
In particular, the various explanations 
of quantum supremacy are...

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.170
I guess I should go to sleep.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:18.940
I'm not used to physical labor. 
It really tired me out.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.390
Then, I guess I'll go to sleep, too.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.460
Jellyfish-san? What's tomorrow's weather?

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.360
Tomorrow will be sunny 
with occasional clouds.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.440
The high temperature is forecast
 to be 25 degrees Celsius.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:33.500
It is likely to be clear, pleasant day.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.760
A good day to go to the beach.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.130
The beach?

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.370
Yeah, the beach.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.350
Really...

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.820
Maybe I'll go, too.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.020
What about your studies?

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.320
Our midterm exams are over.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:53.190
I do have assignments, but it might 
be nice for a change of pace.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.340
Yeah?

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.150
The beach sounds lovely.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.240
Speaking of the beach,

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:02.300
as you know, a sea creature was 
used as the model for my design.

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:00.570
Well, we'll be leaving 
at nine in the morning.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:02.020
Good night, Pudding.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:04.180
Make sure you sleep in your hammock.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.840
Blue skies, white clouds...

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:05.260
Okay.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:08.760
I would very much like to visit 
the real beach just once—

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.800
Well, we'll be going.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.100
See you.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.890
Have a safe trip.

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.030
Please allow me to look after
 the house in your absence.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:25.190
I shall await a souvenir which 
shall make my heart dance as I—

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.740
Oh, good morning!

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.750
Serufu?

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.010
Good morning! Pudding says she'll go, too.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:37.520
What?

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.960
Really?

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.660
You didn't tell me you 
were going with Serufu!

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.230
Let's go! We'll be late!

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:45.160
Wait! Wait, Serufu!

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.680
Isn't it great that the weather's so nice?

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.030
Y-Yes, it's true that the 
weather's nice, but...

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.880
Wait. Let go of me!

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:55.390
Kita Sanjou Station

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:02.430
Getting to go on an outing with 
Suridecchi makes me so happy, meow!

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.910
<i>I had no idea it was a DIY club event.</i>

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.920
<i>Why didn't she tell me that?</i>

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:11.250
To think that Shii-chan is friends 
with Purin. It's like a miracle.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.130
How is this a miracle?

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:16.580
So, why is the DIY club going to the beach?

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:17.980
To gather!

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:18.880
Gather what?

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.080
Hmm...

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.820
Shells and things?

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.040
Driftwood, sea glass...

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:27.380
Things the DIY club can put to good use.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:32.000
Th-Then we'll use them to make pendants, 
brooches, and other little things...

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:36.730
And we'll sell them to raise 
funds for our secret hideout.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.690
It's simply a part of our club activities.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:43.160
Accessories which aren't ready-made, 
and are one-of-a-kind,

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:46.100
make people happier than you might think.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.830
Really? Is that true?

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:50.810
Meow!

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:52.380
Look! Look!

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.650
What is it?

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.850
Wow!

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.750
The beach!

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.790
It's beautiful!

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:18.450
Hmph. Japan's beaches are all right, I guess.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.020
I want to go swimming!

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.970
Hey, we didn't come here to play.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:26.570
Let's split up and look for 
things we might be able to use.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.500
Be careful not to go too far away.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:32.460
Haruko-sensei, is there 
anything you want to add?

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:38.110
Be careful not to cut your hands 
on shells or glass shards.

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:39.690
We will!

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:39.690
Got it!

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:42.660
Suride-san, thank you for your help, too.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:44.420
O-Of course.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:45.620
And now!

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:48.090
We shall each set forth to gather materials!

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.620
Do it...

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.480
...yourself!

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:53.170
Take care out there!

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.180
It's beautiful.

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:09.710
Something like this...

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:13.540
Putting several of them together 
might make cute accessories!

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:16.960
Okay. I'm going to find some more!

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:27.500
Meow?

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.290
You can use that, too?

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:31.720
Y-Yeah.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.350
By combining it with pipes like these,

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.860
it can be used as part of a design 
or in interior design pieces.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:39.780
I see. Like steampunk!

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.730
You're amazing, Leadercchi!

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:42.350
Oh!

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:45.220
Can you use this in something?

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:48.260
How about hanging it from the ceiling 
as an interior design element?

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.720
Oh! That seems kinda fancy!

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.910
These are agate...

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.990
and these are sea glass.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.110
Good.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.200
We should be able to use these.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:05.290
And if we combine them with these shells, 
they might work on headbands or something...

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.090
Oh!

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:08.700
I spy a rock that looks a little weird!

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:14.840
It's a sea cucumber.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:23.550
If I take this home as a souvenir, will it 
make mom and the third generations happy?

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:25.110
Here you are!

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:27.360
Sea cucumber with sanbaizu sauce!

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.680
Thank you for the meal!

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:34.020
It's delicious!

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:39.020
I wonder if there are 
any more sea cucumbers.

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:41.070
Hey, sea cucumbers!

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:42.780
What did you come here for?

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.050
Oh, Purin!

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.780
Purin, will you look for sea cucumbers, too?

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:49.730
Wouldn't that be considered poaching?

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:50.990
Not that I would know.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:55.090
Oh... I wonder if I shouldn't, then.

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:01.620
Bye-bye, sea cucumber!

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:04.270
Don't get caught again, okay?

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.210
Honestly, Serufu is just...

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.370
Will she really do all right 
in the DIY club like that?

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:24.490
Strangely-shaped wood.

00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:28.500
I wonder if it can be used for something.

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:29.910
Something wrong?

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:32.940
Oh, club leader.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:35.410
Oh, that's some nice driftwood.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:38.640
Yes. Since it's got such 
an interesting shape,

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.700
I was wondering if it could 
be used for something.

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:43.650
To best make use of that shape...

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.110
how about a hatrack?

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:47.860
Oh! That might be nice!

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:52.200
But this driftwood is too 
big to take back, isn't it?

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.310
Just a minute.

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:02.650
There. Now we'll be able 
to take it back with us.

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:06.890
Just what one would expect from the 
club leader. You're very skilled.

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.590
It's a question of being familiar with it.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:09.700
Familiar?

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:14.090
No matter how much time passes, Serufu 
probably won't become familiar with any of it.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.260
That's not true.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:19.120
Lately, Serufu seems to have gotten a 
little more familiar with the tools.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.010
What?

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:22.480
She's getting injured less 
often than before, after all.

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:25.770
Really...

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:29.990
If you take these back and sand them 
down, they'll probably be usable.

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:31.890
Would you mind if I take what's left over?

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:34.000
Oh, yes. Please go ahead.

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:36.620
There.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:40.020
You get the perfect attendance 
award, Serufu-san.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:43.450
I cut my finger on a shell.

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:44.370
Meow!

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:47.730
Haru-neechan, this bento you 
made is delicious, meow!

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:53.050
Pudding's mom's ohagi was delicious, but 
for this, you get a "good job," too!

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.540
I'm so glad.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:56.200
Eat as much as you like!

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:58.810
What should we do after this?

00:10:58.810 --> 00:11:01.170
We've gathered quite a 
bit of material, but...

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:02.730
I want to look for some more!

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:03.710
Meow!

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:05.410
I would, too.

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:09.150
After all, I might be able to find something 
even better than I already have.

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:11.470
Pudding, you'll keep looking with us, right?

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:12.530
What?

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:14.870
Well, if it's only for a little while.

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:17.190
That's Suridecchi for you!

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:18.500
Right!

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:20.210
Since we came all the way here,

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:22.650
shall we keep looking a little longer?

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:24.220
Yeah!

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:26.730
Y-Yeah!

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:41.360
I said, this way!

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:42.770
Wait up!

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:47.940
Well, that's probably enough.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.100
We collected quite a bit.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:53.180
With so much, we should be able to 
make a number of different things.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:55.260
Yes! I'm looking forward to it!

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:57.130
What will we make?

00:11:57.620 --> 00:11:59.600
Well then, shall we head back—

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:00.500
Let's play!

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:02.850
Play?

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.260
Build sandcastles...

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:07.730
Swim...

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:09.840
Sunbathe...

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:12.280
And then, and then...

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:16.380
Honestly, coming to the beach and then 
building sandcastles? That's for little kids.

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:21.200
You mentioned swimming, 
but what about swimsuits?

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:23.040
No need to worry about that!

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:29.050
I thought this might happen,
 so I actually wore my swimsuit!

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:30.230
You...

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:32.800
Um, well...

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:36.000
Actually, the thing is...

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:37.230
so did I.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:40.730
You, too, Takumin?

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:44.360
Hmph. You really are hopeless.

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:47.130
I suppose I'll have to go 
along with you, too, then.

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:48.840
Wait, you too, Jobko?

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:51.790
Naturally, I have my swimsuit 
on under my clothes.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.970
What do you mean, "naturally"?

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:56.680
Though, I did wear mine as well!

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:57.800
Why are you doing that?

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.380
Shii, are you...

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:00.050
Meow?

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.480
I guess I don't even need to ask.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:04.670
Which means...

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:05.550
What?

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:09.680
I-I... I was just brought along,

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.200
so there's no way I'd be wearing a—

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.260
She's wearing hers.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:17.850
This morning, she seemed to have lots of fun 
posing in front of the mirror. I saw it.

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:20.440
That's Suridecchi for you!

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:22.690
So everyone was thinking 
the same thing, huh?

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:25.350
Purin, I can't help wondering 
about your swimsuit!

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:27.240
Show us! Show us!

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.280
It's quite cute, isn't it?

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:29.280
H-Hey!

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:38.610
Let's go, baby!

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:39.740
Yay!

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:43.350
Pudding! You didn't bring your 
ninja water spider shoes?!

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:46.180
<b>Water 
Spider Shoes</b>

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:44.510
One of the seven tools of a ninja!

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:46.170
You don't think I actually 
own those, do you?

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:49.080
Jobko-chan, we have the means to use 
the art of water escape, though!

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.130
Really?!

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:51.710
You mean a snorkel, right?

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:54.910
On your marks...

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:58.970
Ready?

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.620
Th-They each seem evenly matched!

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.900
Sh-Shii-san wins!

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:28.060
Meow!

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:28.850
I was so close!

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:30.430
Next time...

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:33.160
Both of you were so fast!

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:35.030
What on earth are they doing?

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:39.680
I'm glad that it's a warm day.

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:43.740
The water's still a little cold, though.

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:47.260
That's true. It feels nice, doesn't it?

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:54.030
What are you doing?

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:58.160
I was wondering if that sea cucumber
 from earlier was around.

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:02.420
A sea cucumber isn't going to take 
you to the Dragon King's palace.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.730
What? Really?

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:06.770
I'm amazed you knew.

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:10.560
Purin, you can see through everything 
when it comes to me, huh?

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:13.480
W-Well, of course!

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:15.770
Knowing what you're thinking is easy.

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:17.660
I'd expect no less from you!

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:21.230
What do you mean, 
"I'd expect no less from you"?

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:23.920
Oh! The way you said that 
sounded just like me!

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:25.260
Try doing it again!

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:26.090
I don't want to.

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:28.580
What? Come on, do it one more time.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:30.200
I said I don't want to!

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:33.420
Finished!

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:37.020
A Japanese castle. Good job, Takumi!

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:40.860
It was worth both of us 
working so hard, wasn't it?

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:43.530
The most important thing is 
the proportion of water.

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:48.070
Really, mixing in clay would 
stabilize the foundation, but...

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.460
Wait, Shii! Behind you!

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.600
The way we depicted the roof 
tiles here, in particular is...

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:52.200
Meow, meow...

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:54.470
Meow?

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:55.430
Huh?

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:57.710
Meow?!

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:06.250
Oh my gosh...

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:11.900
That should do it.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:13.940
Thanks, Purin.

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:17.400
It's been a long time since 
you tied up my hair for me.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.610
If I did it myself, it'd 
come down right away.

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:22.780
Well, you are clumsy, Serufu.

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:28.630
I'm really glad I got to come 
here with you today, Purin.

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:30.210
R-Really?

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:31.960
Really!

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.820
I see.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:39.370
Oh, I know! Say, Purin?

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:40.700
Hm? What?

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:43.850
Purin, why don't you join the DIY club, too?

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:45.360
What?

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:49.770
We go to different high schools, 
but Shii-chan got permission to join.

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:54.490
Purin, if you joined too, we'd be 
able to go home together every day!

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:58.280
You said that it's old and moldy,

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:02.980
but I was wondering if maybe you'd 
sort of taken an interest in it.

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:05.490
But...

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:06.920
But?

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:14.040
Hey! Serufucchi! Suridecchi!

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:17.070
What is it?

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:19.010
Let's all play together!

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.600
Okay! We'll be right there!

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:23.960
Let's go, Purin!

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:29.950
I'm good here.

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:30.950
Huh?

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:33.710
Gathering those materials 
made me a little tired.

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:37.720
Oh... Then, I'll see you later, okay?

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:38.480
Yeah.

00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:51.030
How beautiful.

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:55.720
If I gave this to Serufu, I wonder 
if it would make her happy.

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:09.330
Hmph!

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:36.510
Ow!

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:39.970
Didn't you use sunblock?

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:44.550
How naïve. I came prepared, 
so I'm totally fine.

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:46.470
Oh, that stupid beach! I never—

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:47.950
Never should have gone?

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:52.230
No, it's not that, but...

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:55.170
It's not like it wasn't fun...

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:56.940
What? I can't hear you!

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.160
It's nothing!

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:11.000
There!

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.450
It's all done!

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.290
It's a masterpiece if I do 
say so myself, meow!

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:19.280
Later, put it back the way it was.

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:20.040
Meow?!

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:22.440
Then...

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:25.670
I think I'll make bracelets 
out of the sea glass.

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:27.500
You're going to use this 
to drill holes in them?

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:28.680
Yes.

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:33.020
First, we'll put a little water 
on the face of the sea glass.

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:34.590
Why water?

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:38.570
When you cut into sea glass, 
glass dust will fly off of it...

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:41.050
and the heat can make it crack more easily.

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:42.480
Really?

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.440
I'm going to start carving now.

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:52.410
Once the water turns a cloudy white...

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:54.630
please rinse it lightly with more water.

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:57.590
Once the hole has gone about
 80% of the way through...

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:00.330
switch to a 2mm diamond bit...

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:02.540
and then start drilling from the other side.

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:08.420
Once the hole is done, paint 
the front with resin...

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.850
and harden it using a UV light.

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:15.300
Then, thread the sea glass and some 
beads on a nylon beading string...

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:18.070
and it's done!

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:20.480
Wow!

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:22.100
Takumin, you're amazing!

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:24.850
It's really like something 
a shop might sell!

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:26.820
Good job, Takumi!

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:30.080
Takumicchi, you've got skills!

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:33.790
It's true. You could sell these 
anywhere and not be embarrassed.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:37.250
R-Really? I'm so glad!

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:40.960
So, how are we going to 
sell them? Over the internet?

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:45.670
Let's sell them not just in Japan,
 but internationally too, meow!

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:50.020
Maybe we'll get a flood of orders 
from all over the world!

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:50.950
That's dreaming a little too big.

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:56.350
Aside from the internet, there's the 
culture festival bazaar, but that's in the fall.

00:20:56.640 --> 00:20:57.890
How about flea markets?

00:20:57.890 --> 00:21:01.020
Some shops have tables for rent.

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:03.830
They sell handicrafts and things there.

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:05.710
That could work, too.

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:09.530
Wait. I might be able to ask if we 
could set them up in our store.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:13.000
Open

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:12.670
What? In Waku Waku Wan Wan?

00:21:12.990 --> 00:21:15.640
I'd like to go there! To Waku Wan!

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:16.420
Huh?

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:18.940
Leadercchi, I want to go to your house!

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:20.210
Oh.

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:23.540
Sure. You should all come over and hang out.

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:25.360
Yay!

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:36.590
Rain.

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:42.680
It's just right.

00:21:42.680 --> 00:21:45.340
Pretty impressive for a first try.

00:21:45.340 --> 00:21:48.060
I still have sea glass 
and shells left, so...

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.740
Maybe I can use them to make some 
kind of decorative object...

00:21:51.230 --> 00:21:54.290
Wait. What am I doing?

00:21:58.300 --> 00:21:59.970
I have to study.

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Step 7</b>

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>"DIY" Means You Can Do Things Inside If It's Gloomy Out</b>
